{"case_id": "r1pdf:826cdb765c276ba900010084", "input_sha256": "70499ae231a78277dd0955c6c31299e437c033b39c4194ad4f7f23c8bbe3b321", "raw_output": "```json\n{\n  \"evidence_ids\": [\n    \"D01:S01\",\n    \"D01:S05\"\n  ],\n  \"quotes\": [\n    {\n      \"evidence_id\": \"D01:S01\",\n      \"quote\": \"A and T indicate specific neuropathologic changes that define Alzheimer’s disease, \\nwhereas (N) and (C) are not specific to Alzheimer’s disease and are therefore placed in \\nparentheses.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"evidence_id\": \"D01:S05\",\n      \"quote\": \"For these reasons, we have placed (N) in parenthesis, indicating the fundamental \\ndifferences between (N) and AT.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"reason\": \"证据D01:S01和D01:S05支持目标引用中关于在研究框架中将(N)置于括号内以强调其非特异性的主张。D01:S01明确指出A和T指示定义AD的特异性神经病理变化，而(N)和(C)对AD不特异，因此被置于括号中。D01:S05进一步说明(N)生物标志物不映射到用于诊断AD的神经病理发现，并重申将(N)置于括号中表明其与AT之间的根本差异。这些证据直接支持了目标引用中关于(N)非特异性及括号使用理由的主张，但未涵盖目标引用中提到的'2018研究框架'这一具体时间背景，仅提供了框架内容的证据。\"\n}\n```", "attempted": true, "observed_input": {"input_tokens": 2838, "required_total": 3350, "input_ids_sha256": "945650d2cadf9e8c85fbecf3609d87410b09dfd3022bbc3d986ecf011cbb8dda", "within_budget": true, "truncation": false, "generated_token_ids": [71093, 2164, 198, 90, 198, 220, 328, 68, 26590, 7824, 763, 498, 198, 262, 328, 35, 15, 16, 72799, 15, 16, 487, 198, 262, 328, 35, 15, 16, 72799, 15, 20, 1, 198, 220, 10339, 198, 220, 328, 51492, 763, 498, 198, 262, 313, 198, 406, 328, 68, 26590, 816, 763, 328, 35, 15, 16, 72799, 15, 16, 487, 198, 406, 328, 2855, 763, 328, 32, 321, 345, 12832, 3050, 94199, 572, 36866, 4203, 421, 6762, 41995, 725, 8197, 11, 1088, 77, 2777, 299, 318, 45, 8, 321, 318, 34, 8, 513, 524, 3050, 310, 41995, 725, 8197, 321, 513, 8646, 8826, 303, 1088, 77, 39708, 37052, 1149, 198, 262, 2390, 198, 262, 313, 198, 406, 328, 68, 26590, 816, 763, 328, 35, 15, 16, 72799, 15, 20, 487, 198, 406, 328, 2855, 763, 328, 2381, 1439, 7715, 11, 567, 599, 8826, 318, 45, 8, 303, 92062, 11, 18290, 279, 15346, 1088, 302,